		{"id":"753cf89b0e4f1521","type":"group","x":-320,"y":-1080,"width":840,"height":545,"color":"#1068c6","label":"Steam Controller"},
		{"id":"5747e8fdb90861ec","type":"file","file":"Semester 2/Interface Design/Tasks/Challenge 1/attachments/Pasted image 20260314165248.png","x":186,"y":-850,"width":175,"height":139},
		{"id":"03de1559d78ecc23","type":"text","text":"- Play & Immersion\n- Game Controller\n\n\n","x":171,"y":-993,"width":205,"height":61,"color":"#1068c6"},
		{"id":"279d1f010c98e374","type":"file","file":"Semester 2/Interface Design/Tasks/Challenge 1/attachments/Pasted image 20260314170649.png","x":855,"y":293,"width":400,"height":202},
		{"id":"1017ff1cabcf99f6","type":"text","text":"- Creation & Operation\n- Desktop","x":240,"y":767,"width":250,"height":60,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"f49f50b06147677d","type":"file","file":"Semester 2/Interface Design/Tasks/Challenge 1/attachments/Pasted image 20260314170612.png","x":606,"y":296,"width":188,"height":199},
		{"id":"d18869a38eb45368","type":"text","text":"**Effectiveness / Efficiency**\nMost important git functions are easily accessible in the ui\n**Satisfaction**\nIt isn’t really “satisfying” in the general sense, because it’s only there to assist with commits, and ideally, the developer shouldn’t get distracted.\n**Learnability / Memorability**\nIf you’re familiar with git, the Github Desktop interface is simple to learn and use.\n**Safety**\nThere are confirmation pop ups, but you can easily lose a lot of work if you’re being a little clumsy! That usually doesn’t happen though in day to day use.\n\n\n","x":760,"y":687,"width":438,"height":390,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"211dfb4af79a3718","type":"text","text":"#### Steam Controller","x":148,"y":-640,"width":250,"height":60,"color":"#1068c6"},
		{"id":"0166f4a98aae8aae","type":"text","text":"## The Good","x":-9,"y":-118,"width":249,"height":85,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"1c298a92a8246e7b","type":"text","text":"**Effectiveness / Efficiency**\nThe Steam Controller is very effective and efficient to use once you learn how to use it. It’s incredible, especially for any mouse interfaces!\n**Satisfaction**\nIt is satisfying to use, but due to its age, the vibration motor and tactile feelings isn’t up to modern standards.\n**Learnability / Memorability**\nDifficult. It’s very different to a normal controller, since instead of a stick and dpad, it uses two touch pads. \n**Safety**\nThere is nothing to report here.\n\n\n","x":-275,"y":-1020,"width":368,"height":411,"color":"#1068c6"},
		{"id":"fa844296f4c68b5b","type":"file","file":"Semester 2/Interface Design/Tasks/Challenge 1/attachments/Pasted image 20260314170600.png","x":236,"y":309,"width":320,"height":172},
		{"id":"3b1d635dc059445b","type":"text","text":"#### Github Desktop","x":236,"y":557,"width":250,"height":60,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"1a3e2f19ba208f76","type":"text","text":"#### Zoe’s Blender","x":-410,"y":321,"width":250,"height":60,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"9082a3903e9f8695","type":"file","file":"Semester 2/Interface Design/Tasks/Challenge 1/attachments/Pasted image 20260314171811.png","x":-1360,"y":267,"width":300,"height":400},
		{"id":"1c83a780433877f3","type":"file","file":"Semester 2/Interface Design/Tasks/Challenge 1/attachments/Pasted image 20260314171826.png","x":-1360,"y":707,"width":300,"height":400},
		{"id":"61b0416c9350d04c","type":"file","file":"Semester 2/Interface Design/Tasks/Challenge 1/attachments/Pasted image 20260314171832.png","x":-1032,"y":707,"width":300,"height":400},
		{"id":"c6c1cbbd407aac3e","type":"text","text":"- Consumption & Lifestyle\n- Blender\n\n\n","x":-940,"y":308,"width":415,"height":86,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"f780b41731aaa346","type":"text","text":"**Effectiveness / Efficiency**\nThis blender just requires you to put the cup in and push and twist. Gets teh job done\n**Satisfaction**\nIt’s very satisfying to use! \n**Learnability / Memorability**\nIncredibly easy to learn since it just push and twist! The twist is optional even! \n**Safety**\nI haven’t figured out a way how to hurt yourself during regular operation of the device.\n\n\n","x":-598,"y":707,"width":438,"height":310,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"230a3b38bb66a5ad","type":"text","text":"- Play & Immersion\n- Desktop Game (Space Sim)\n\n\n","x":-760,"y":-231,"width":280,"height":79,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"3e1b1c3576b4ebe6","type":"file","file":"Semester 2/Interface Design/Tasks/Challenge 1/attachments/20210201205420_1.jpg","x":-1760,"y":-876,"width":400,"height":225},
		{"id":"66f83dd3c23341f6","type":"file","file":"Semester 2/Interface Design/Tasks/Challenge 1/attachments/20211001230800_1.jpg","x":-1760,"y":-584,"width":400,"height":225},
		{"id":"743b3bd99aacb844","type":"file","file":"Semester 2/Interface Design/Tasks/Challenge 1/attachments/359320_20260120221056_1.png","x":-1760,"y":-1162,"width":400,"height":225},
		{"id":"44cbb1e68c156dc4","type":"text","text":"#### Elite: Dangerous","x":-1160,"y":-191,"width":250,"height":60,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"b2e043ddb2776847","type":"file","file":"Semester 2/Interface Design/Tasks/Challenge 1/attachments/20250301203718_1.jpg","x":-1760,"y":-304,"width":400,"height":225},
		{"id":"8d89c278d5c98655","type":"text","text":"**Effectiveness / Efficiency**\nMost Elite: Dangerous players play the game using a HOTAS *(Hands on Throttle and Stick)*. So the ship UI is designed to work well when using one. The entire UI is easily navigable using just the hat of a HOTAS. It’s easy and fast to achieve whatever you’re trying to do. \n**Satisfaction**\nThe UI sounds are incredibly satisfying.\n**Learnability / Memorability**\nUnfortunately, it takes a long time to learn, due to the large amount of features and options you have in your ship. That holds true for the entire game. \n**Safety**\nThere is minimal safety, you can easily make a mistake, like for example ejecting a valuable piece of cargo. But this usually isn’t a big issue. \n\n\n\n","x":-1142,"y":-792,"width":520,"height":425,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"4de8a4627cfe8ad4","type":"file","file":"Semester 2/Interface Design/Tasks/Challenge 1/attachments/Pasted image 20260314174239.png","x":3680,"y":-1511,"width":400,"height":221},
		{"id":"02d129307146a513","type":"file","file":"Semester 2/Interface Design/Tasks/Challenge 1/attachments/ScreenShot-2024-05-12_11-57-31-18A.jpg","x":3680,"y":-850,"width":400,"height":225},
		{"id":"8740245b7b1346f8","type":"file","file":"Semester 2/Interface Design/Tasks/Challenge 1/attachments/ScreenShot-2024-08-29_18-11-23-4D6.jpg","x":3680,"y":-1197,"width":400,"height":225},
		{"id":"9c673af84b1908be","type":"file","file":"Semester 2/Interface Design/Tasks/Challenge 1/attachments/ScreenShot-2026-02-20_19-32-24-ED2.jpg","x":4175,"y":-1511,"width":400,"height":225},
		{"id":"a681a1fed7004633","type":"text","text":"**Effectiveness / Efficiency**\nN/A - Same as regular \n**Satisfaction**\nNot satisfying due to getting in the way\n**Learnability / Memorability**\nN/A\n**Safety**\nN/A\n\n\n\n","x":4360,"y":602,"width":438,"height":235,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"aedb03469a355495","type":"text","text":"- Consumption & Lifestyle\n- Food","x":4051,"y":738,"width":250,"height":60,"color":"1"},
